  "definition": "Precision is the fraction of predicted positive cases that are actually positive: TP/(TP+FP). It penalizes false positives. It is used in Classification Evaluation. It is commonly considered alongside Classification Accuracy, Confusion Matrix, Recall.",
  "intuition": "Think of Precision as a summary number: it compresses many outcomes into one interpretable value so you can compare models or decisions.",
